<!-- SYNTHETIC FIXTURE: fully fictional data (Musterberatung GmbH).
     UBL Invoice, XRechnung 3.0 CIUS, expected VALID (clean) under the German
     profile. This is the NOT-SUBJECT-TO-VAT fixture (VAT category O): a German
     consultancy invoicing for a supply that falls OUTSIDE the scope of VAT (a
     nicht steuerbarer Umsatz — the place of supply is outside the Union, so no
     EU VAT arises at all). Every line carries VAT category code O ('Services
     outside scope of tax') and the invoice shows ZERO VAT.

     Category O is the structural ODD ONE OUT — its BR-O family is a set of
     PROHIBITIONS, so this fixture deliberately OMITS what every other category
     requires:
       * NO VAT registration identifier ANYWHERE: the Seller has NO VAT-scheme
         PartyTaxScheme/CompanyID (BT-31) and the Buyer none (BT-48), because
         BR-O-02 forbids a Seller/tax-representative/Buyer VAT identifier on an
         O invoice. The Seller is instead identified by its BT-30 legal
         registration id (PartyLegalEntity/CompanyID = HRB 00003), which alone
         satisfies BR-CO-26. Since O is NOT in the BR-DE-16 trigger set
         (S/Z/E/AE/K/G/L/M), the missing seller tax id does not trip BR-DE-16.
       * NO LINE VAT RATE: the O invoice lines carry NO cbc:Percent element,
         because BR-O-05 forbids a line VAT rate (BT-152). The BG-23 VAT
         BREAKDOWN, however, DOES carry BT-119 = 0: the German CIUS BR-DE-14 is
         stricter than the EN core and mandates a non-empty VAT category rate in
         EVERY breakdown row with no O carve-out (no BR-O rule forbids the
         breakdown rate, only the line rate), so a pure-O XRechnung needs it.
       * exactly ONE BG-23 VAT breakdown, category O ONLY (BR-O-11/12/13/14
         exclusivity — no other VAT category anywhere), BT-116 taxable = Σ O
         line nets, BT-117 tax amount = 0.00 (BR-O-08/09),
       * the mandated out-of-scope exemption reason on that breakdown: BT-121
         code VATEX-EU-O (on the CEF VATEX list, BR-CL-22) AND the BT-120 reason
         text (BR-O-10, presence-required).
     BT-84 is the ISO 13616 documentation example IBAN (valid check digits), so
     the German SEPA IBAN check (BR-DE-19) is satisfied and the invoice is clean.

     ARITHMETIC (all internally consistent, EUR, VAT = 0 throughout):
       line 1 (O): 1  x 5000.00 = 5000.00 -> BT-131 = 5000.00
       line 2 (O): 10 x  250.00 = 2500.00 -> BT-131 = 2500.00
       BT-106 sum of line nets = 5000 + 2500                  = 7500.00
       O breakdown base BT-116 = 5000 + 2500 = 7500.00 -> BT-117 = 0.00
       BT-109 tax exclusive = 7500.00 = sole breakdown base
       BT-110 total VAT = 0.00
       BT-112 tax inclusive = 7500.00 + 0.00 = 7500.00 = BT-115 payable -->
